course: dictionary
lesson: 5195
title: Jagged edges
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Jagged means rough, sharp and uneven, with points or edges that are not smooth. Think of a broken bottle or the teeth of a saw. The context often shows you the meaning: «The leaves have jagged teeth.» Teeth are sharp, so jagged teeth must be sharp and uneven.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The leaves have sharp, uneven teeth» still makes sense, so jagged means the same kind of thing. A smooth or round word would not fit, so it must mean rough and pointy.
explain: Writers use jagged to paint pictures. «The sand tiger shark looks fierce with its long jagged teeth.» The teeth look scary because they are sharp and uneven. Jagged is also used for mountains, peaks and lightning, so you can picture a shape that is sharp and not smooth.
explain: Jagged can be a warning too. Jagged glass can cut you, so never touch it. When you see jagged, ask yourself: is this sharp and rough, and could it hurt me?
fact: Jagged means rough, sharp and uneven, with points or edges.
fact: Jagged is an adjective. You can say more jagged to compare two things.
fact: The word jagged can describe teeth, edges, rocks, peaks or lightning.
fact: «The name dandelion comes from French words meaning lion's tooth, because the leaves have jagged teeth.»
fact: Jagged glass is dangerous, so be careful and do not touch broken glass.
exercise: «The leaves have jagged teeth.» What does jagged mean? | Smooth and shiny | Soft and warm | *Rough, sharp and uneven | Round and even
exercise: «The sand tiger shark looks fierce with its long jagged teeth.» Why does the shark look fierce? | It has no teeth at all | Its teeth are soft and round | It is very small and quick | *Its teeth are sharp and uneven
exercise: Which word means about the same as jagged? | smooth | *rough | round | soft
test: «Snow covered the jagged peaks above the village.» What does jagged tell you about the peaks? | *Sharp and uneven | Smooth and rounded | Low and flat | Warm and soft
test: «Dandelion flowers close at night and in rain.» Which word in the sentence is about the leaves? | rain | dandelion | *leaves | flowers
exam: Mia says, «The broken bottle has jagged edges.» What should she do? | *Take care, because the sharp, uneven edges can cut you | Lick the edge to see if it is smooth | Put it in her pocket | Pick it up and hold it tightly
